.TH BITTY 1 "September 2026" "bitty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bitty \- set Conway's Game of Life loose in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bitty
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bitty is an interactive Game of Life editor and simulator. It renders two Life
rows in each terminal row using Unicode half blocks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --density " N"
Initial live-cell density from 0 through 1 (default 0.25).
.TP
.BI --speed " N"
Generations per second from 1 through 60 (default 12).
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Random seed. The current time is used by default.
.TP
.BI --width " N"
World width. Defaults to the terminal width.
.TP
.BI --height " N"
World height. Defaults to twice the available terminal height.
.TP
.BI --wrap=false
Treat cells beyond the world edges as dead.
.TP
.B --paused
Start paused.
.TP
.BR --intro , --no-intro
Force or suppress the once-per-version startup animation.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B --version
Print version information.
.SH KEYS
Arrow keys or hjkl move; space toggles a cell; p pauses; n steps; r randomizes;
c clears; + and - change speed; w toggles wrapping; q quits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
BITTY_STATE_DIR, BITTY_THEME_FILE, BITTY_INTRO_ALWAYS, BITTY_NO_INTRO,
BITTY_NO_COLOR, and NO_COLOR are recognized.
